  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758875,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1 Year of Deathray: A Commodore 64 Blast from the Past\n\nPrepare for a frantic, pixelated onslaught in *1 Year of Deathray*, a fast-paced shoot 'em up for the Commodore 64! Set in a bizarre alternate 1943, the world is under siege from hordes of robotic invaders armed with devastating deathrays. You pilot a heavily armed experimental fighter, the \"Phoenix,\" tasked with pushing back the mechanical menace and uncovering the source of the invasion.\n\nGameplay is a relentless barrage of enemy ships, laser fire, and explosive power-ups. Navigate through vibrant, scrolling landscapes, from futuristic cityscapes to treacherous volcanic islands, collecting upgrades to enhance your firepower and defenses. Master the Phoenix’s signature loop maneuver to dodge incoming attacks, but be warned – you only have a limited number of lives! \n\nFeaturing a catchy chiptune soundtrack and stunning (for the time) graphics, *1 Year of Deathray* delivers a challenging and rewarding arcade experience that will test your reflexes and strategic thinking. Can you survive a year of deathrays and save the world?"
    },
